From: conda-forge hkl-feedstock maintainers
Date: 2026-05-27
Subject: Make api2/ + ccan coroutine/generator conditional on <ucontext.h>

`hkl/api2/hkl2.h` unconditionally includes
`hkl/ccan/generator/generator.h`, which in turn includes
`hkl/ccan/coroutine/coroutine.h`.  generator.h contains:

    #if !COROUTINE_AVAILABLE
    #error Generators require coroutines
    #endif

and COROUTINE_AVAILABLE is true iff HAVE_UCONTEXT is true.

On Windows (MinGW or MSVC) there is no <ucontext.h>, so HAVE_UCONTEXT
is 0, COROUTINE_AVAILABLE is 0, and any build that includes generator.h
fails.  The api2/ subdir cannot be built on Windows for this reason.

On macOS 11+, ucontext.h exists but the routines are POSIX 2008-
deprecated and the ccan probe's runtime test aborts (small probe stack
< MINSIGSTKSZ).  This is why hkl-feedstock cross-builds osx-* from
linux-64 rather than natively on macOS.

This patch decouples the api2/ subdir from the rest of the build by
adding a configure-time check for <ucontext.h> and conditionalising:

  - `SUBDIRS += api2` in `hkl/Makefile.am`
  - the `coroutine/*` and `generator/*` entries in
    `libccan_la_SOURCES` in `hkl/ccan/Makefile.am`

When <ucontext.h> is absent, neither the api2 sublibrary nor the
coroutine/generator ccan modules are built.  The rest of libhkl
(including hkl-binding.c, hkl-factory.c, the diffractometer engines,
and the GObject-Introspection scanning) is unaffected and works
identically.

Note that the `configurator` ccan helper also has a HAVE_UCONTEXT
probe in `ccan_config.h` (it compiles + runs a test program).  We
do NOT remove that probe; it still runs and writes ccan_config.h.
The two HAVE_UCONTEXT values (autoconf's vs configurator's) will
agree on every platform we care about because they both ultimately
ask the C preprocessor whether <ucontext.h> can be #included.

Upstream alternative (cleaner, but more invasive): add a Win32
Fibers backend for ccan/coroutine.  Either approach would render
this patch unnecessary.

This patch is carried in `hkl-feedstock` while we discuss the right
direction with the upstream maintainer; it can be dropped once an
upstream solution lands and the recipe pins the fixed commit.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -232,6 +232,22 @@ GOBJECT_INTROSPECTION_CHECK([0.6.7])
 AM_COND_IF([HAVE_INTROSPECTION],
         [PKG_CHECK_MODULES([GOBJECT], [gobject-2.0])])
 
+dnl ***************************
+dnl *** api2 / coroutine    ***
+dnl ***************************
+dnl
+dnl The api2 sublibrary (trajectory_gen via ccan's generator + coroutine)
+dnl requires <ucontext.h> with working getcontext/makecontext/setcontext/
+dnl swapcontext.  These are POSIX 2008-DEPRECATED and unavailable on
+dnl Windows (MinGW/MSVC have no ucontext API).  When ucontext.h is not
+dnl present, skip building the api2/ subdir and the generator/coroutine
+dnl sources entirely.  This is recipe-driven for now (hkl-feedstock
+dnl patch 0003); an upstream fix would supply a Win32 Fibers backend for
+dnl ccan/coroutine or otherwise decouple api2/ from coroutine availability.
+AC_CHECK_HEADERS([ucontext.h], [have_ucontext=yes], [have_ucontext=no])
+AM_CONDITIONAL([HAVE_API2], [test x$have_ucontext = xyes])
+
+
 
 dnl ***************
 dnl *** contrib ***
--- a/hkl/Makefile.am
+++ b/hkl/Makefile.am
@@ -1,5 +1,8 @@
 ## Process this file with automake to produce Makefile.in
-SUBDIRS = ccan . api2
+SUBDIRS = ccan .
+if HAVE_API2
+SUBDIRS += api2
+endif
 
 AM_CFLAGS = \
 	-Wno-initializer-overrides \
--- a/hkl/ccan/Makefile.am
+++ b/hkl/ccan/Makefile.am
@@ -23,12 +23,8 @@ libccan_la_SOURCES = \
 	check_type/check_type.h \
 	compiler/compiler.h \
 	container_of/container_of.h \
-	coroutine/coroutine.c \
-	coroutine/coroutine.h \
 	cppmagic/cppmagic.h \
 	darray/darray.h \
-	generator/generator.c \
-	generator/generator.h \
 	list/list.c \
 	list/list.h \
 	ptrint/ptrint.h \
@@ -38,6 +34,14 @@ libccan_la_SOURCES = \
 	str/str.h \
 	typesafe_cb/typesafe_cb.h
 
+if HAVE_API2
+libccan_la_SOURCES += \
+	coroutine/coroutine.c \
+	coroutine/coroutine.h \
+	generator/generator.c \
+	generator/generator.h
+endif
+
 ccanincludedir=$(includedir)/hkl-@VMAJ@/hkl/ccan
 nobase_ccaninclude_HEADERS= \
 	darray/darray.h
